{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"4","amends":"clause","what":"The Context's `cli.ts` sentence \"calls `promote(…, process.cwd(), CLOCK)`\" — implemented as a `here()` helper that prefers `process.env.npm_config_local_prefix` when `process.cwd()` is the repository root, falling back to `process.cwd()` otherwise.","why":"Measured on Bun 1.4.0: `bun run <script>` chdirs into the package root before running the script and does not set `INIT_CWD`, so a bare `process.cwd()` inside cli.ts is the repository root however the child was spawned — `bun run history promote` spawned with `cwd` a temp directory would write into the repo root, not that directory, contradicting M3's \"under the current directory\" and Proof leg (g). The directory the invocation actually came from is what bun leaves in `npm_config_local_prefix`. Reading it only when `process.cwd()` is the repo root (exactly the case where bun did the chdir) keeps a direct `bun packages/tinyapp-history/src/cli.ts` run writing where it stands and stops a stale inherited variable from ever overriding a real cwd. Verified both spawn shapes write the three files into the spawn's own directory, byte-identical to the committed ones.","id":"01M2MBPA4P0000J541T3M2QGK0","ts":1789537233046}
